vectors.json: yarl's URL(), str() and join(), urljoin, and RobotFileParser's can_fetch and crawl_delay on hand-picked cases, recorded with Python 3.14.4 and aiohttp 3.13.5. chain/: the JSON-RPC answers of a `bulk bittensor-fetch --only-chain --block 9491485` run recorded through examples/rpc_record.rs, each block cut to its first extrinsic; expected/: the golden chain snapshot and registration dates at that block. replay/: the HTTP exchanges of a live fetch of subnets 2, 6, 20, 39, 45, 50, 101, 120, 122 and 128, with blocks cut to their first extrinsic and synthetic hosts and subnets 900-904 added; input/ holds the chain snapshot and a synthetic previous fetch; expected/ and stdout.txt: the golden fetch against examples/fetch_replay.rs serving replay.json.gz, with input/previous as the previous fetch. Read by bulk/bittensor/tests/fetch.rs.
